### 3. Auth & User Services (.NET Core)

#### [MODIFY] [AuthService.cs](file:///d:/shivam/doctor-appointment-system/DoctorAppointmentSystem/DoctorAppointmentSystem/Application/Services/AuthService.cs)
- Update `RegisterAsync`:
  1. Validate that at least one channel is filled.
  2. Check existing DB records for Email / Mobile conflicts. If duplicate exists, throw clear exception (*"This email/WhatsApp is already registered. Please log in."*).
  3. Dispatch Email OTP / WhatsApp OTP to requested channels.
- Implement `LoginWithWhatsAppOtpAsync`: Verify WhatsApp OTP from Redis cache, load User, and generate JWT token.

#### [MODIFY] [PatientService.cs](file:///d:/shivam/doctor-appointment-system/DoctorAppointmentSystem/DoctorAppointmentSystem/Application/Services/PatientService.cs)
- Implement `InitiateUpdateContactInfoAsync` & `ConfirmUpdateContactInfoAsync`:
  1. Verify uniqueness of new Email / WhatsApp number.
  2. Send OTP to the **NEW** Email/WhatsApp address.
  3. Upon verification, replace active contact info on `User` & `Patient`.
  4. Write log to `AuditLogs` (*"Email updated from old@domain.com to new@domain.com"*).
  5. Send security alert notification to old channel.

